  {
    "kind": "youtube#playlistItem",
    "etag": "\"nxOHAKTVB7baOKsQgTtJIyGxcs8/YM2YrS888pqGxVYO--YAjXh9Er8\"",
    "id": "VVVzS3hacXJaYlY1UjlFaEhLOC1hQnp3Ljk4STNfRG5BUXZv",
    "snippet": {
      "publishedAt": "2015-11-04T07:35:29.000Z",
      "channelId": "UCsKxZqrZbV5R9EhHK8-aBzw",
      "title": "Martin Naumann – 3D on the web: WebGL and WebVR – Falsy Values 2015",
      "description": "http://falsyvalues.com/\n\nThe modern web is tearing down the borders of the browser window and allows us to create so much more than just another website.\nThis talk is a whirlwind tour of how 3D and virtual reality can be woven into entirely new applications that the web hasn’t seen yet. On top of interactive 3D web applications with WebGL we’ll go through the history of 3D on the web.\nIn addition we’ll see how we can unlock the powers of the GPU thanks to GLSL.\nWe will then explore the amazing superpowers that Virtual Reality is currently bringing to the web and teleport us to places we can’t go.\nThis is going to be accompanied with live coding 3D demos and weave them together with other web technologies such as WebRTC and Web Audio and lots of show cases and demos to give you inspiration on what to build with your freshly-learned tricks and know-how.",
